module Core

### Represents the protocol for saturating division.
### `ClampingDivisible` is for bounded numeric types whose division surface can
### clamp representable overflow conditions instead of propagating them as hard
### failure or undefined behavior.
protocol ClampingDivisible
  ### Returns the clamping quotient of this value and `you`.
  ### Implementations should preserve normal division semantics when the exact
  ### quotient is representable and clamp only the out-of-range result cases.
  ### :param you: The other value to divide by.
  ### :returns: The resulting `Me` value.
  @readonly
  routine Me.$truediv_clamp(you: Me) -> ?Me
